ivtc_opencl: add hardware inverse-telecine (field matching) through OpenCL

New filter `ivtc_opencl` performing 3:2 field-matching inverse telecine on the
GPU, designed for the zero-copy QSV decode -> OpenCL -> QSV encode chain:

  hwmap=derive_device=opencl, ivtc_opencl, hwmap=derive_device=qsv:reverse=1

Field matching is a faithful OpenCL port of vf_fieldmatch's compare_fields
(default mode pc_n, C-vs-P primary): per frame three chained kernels compute the
inter-field motion mask and the masked [1 4 1] combing energy on the GPU
(opencl/ivtc.cl: fm_absdiff -> fm_diffmap = build_diff_map -> fm_compare_accum,
all in 0..255 luma units so fieldmatch's integer thresholds apply unchanged),
and a single readback brings back per-work-group accumulators; the host runs
compare_fields' scalar tier decision (ivtc_decide). This GPU-accumulate /
host-decide split keeps matching to ONE GPU<->CPU sync per frame. The chosen
match is woven by ivtc_synthesize. Matched frames feed a 5-frame cycle;
decimation drops the most-redundant one using vf_decimate's metric -- the
minimum *maxbdiff* (max localized 32x32-block diff), with totdiff/dupthresh/
scthresh selection (ivtc_diff emits per-block sums; the host reduces them) --
yielding 23.976 CFR from 29.97 telecine. Soft pulldown is handled too: qsv
strips repeat_pict, but the 2:3 cadence survives in the inter-frame PTS spans,
so each input frame is re-tiled onto the display-field grid by its real span (a
3-field frame feeds an extra copy) -- rebuilding the ~30p stream the matcher and
5:4 decimation invert exactly. Hard telecine / true 30p have uniform spans, so
one feed per frame: that path is unchanged. Kept frames are emitted on a
contiguous 23.976 grid (first frame anchored to the input PTS, then free-run +1)
so the output has no holes for a CFR/HLS muxer to dup-fill (the cause of a ~19%
duplicate judder on soft-telecined broadcast); the kept-frame count matches the
content duration, so A/V stays synced. Output is
allocated from an own OpenCL pool (ff_opencl_filter_config_output2) so it
reverse-maps cleanly to a QSV encoder; the matched output is flagged
progressive. Kernels use the AV_PIX_FMT_OPENCL image2d_t model (normalized
read_imagef, bit-depth agnostic).

Credit: the field-matching algorithm and the OpenCL kernels are ported from
QSVEnc (QSVPipeline/rgy_filter_ivtc) by rigaya, used under the MIT License
(QSVEnc/NVEnc/VCEEnc, Copyright (c) 2014-2016 rigaya,
https://github.com/rigaya/QSVEnc). The OpenCL filter scaffolding follows
FFmpeg's vf_bwdif_opencl.c (Copyright (c) 2025 NyanMisaka).

Validated end-to-end on Intel hardware: exact 5->4 decimation, progressive
24000/1001 output, no host copies, one GPU sync per frame. The compare_fields
port was verified faithful by instrumenting software fieldmatch: the GPU
accumulators match SW's per-frame values, and the decimated output is identical
to software fieldmatch,decimate frame-for-frame (100% in a test pan, ~98% over
60s including high-motion). The earlier hard 1-frame judder is resolved.

Status (checkpoint): on recorded clips this filter's output equals software
fieldmatch,decimate frame-for-frame (smooth). A "reduced-frames" stutter seen
on the LIVE stream was traced to input frame-delivery gaps being turned into
duplicate frames by the old free-running-grid + drift-guard emit (it accumulated
drift and then jumped, bunching the dup-fill into bursts); the input-PTS-tracking
emit above replaces it to spread that compensation. Not yet validated under
clean live reception (local capture/curl drops frames in bursts, masking it).
Deferred: deinterlace fallback for genuinely-interlaced / non-telecine sections.

Note: on Meteor Lake the zero-copy VA-API<->OpenCL surface mapping
(cl_intel_va_api_media_sharing) currently misreads Tile4 surfaces in the Intel
compute runtime, corrupting any neighbour-reading OpenCL filter (this one and
the in-tree bwdif_opencl alike); until that is fixed upstream, route the OpenCL
stage through system memory (hwdownload/hwupload) instead of hwmap.

Deferred: compare_fields mN/scene-change (checkmm) fallback and chroma in the
match metric (SW uses C/P only with chroma off-by-default-negligible here),
BWDIF/deinterlace fallback for truly-interlaced / non-clean-telecine sections.

Files: libavfilter/vf_ivtc_opencl.c, libavfilter/opencl/ivtc.cl (new),
libavfilter/allfilters.c, libavfilter/Makefile, configure,
libavfilter/opencl_source.h.

